# 🎯 Decorator Implementation Patterns

## Standard Decorator Structure
```typescript
export function decoratorName(options?: DecoratorOptions) {
  return function (target: any, propertyKey: string, descriptor: PropertyDescriptor) {
    const originalMethod = descriptor.value;
    
    descriptor.value = async function (...args: any[]) {
      // Pre-execution logic
      try {
        const result = await originalMethod.apply(this, args);
        // Post-execution logic
        return result;
      } catch (error) {
        // Error handling
        throw error;
      } finally {
        // Cleanup logic
      }
    };
    
    return descriptor;
  };
}
```

## Required Imports
- Import `globalLogger` for error logging
- Import `globalTracker` for metrics collection
- Use relative imports for project utilities

## Key Generation
- Always use format: `${target.constructor.name}.${propertyKey}`
- Include method arguments in cache keys when needed
- Keep keys consistent across decorators

## Async/Sync Handling
- Check `originalMethod.constructor.name.includes('AsyncFunction')` for async detection
- Handle both patterns in cache decorator
- Always await async methods properly

